    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>From a city near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayacucho">Ayacucho</a>, Wari spread planned administrative centres and colonies across highland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> between about 600 and 1000.</li><li>Its tapestry tunics, pottery and Staff God imagery travelled widely, and feasts with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maize">maize</a> and molle beer helped bind local leaders to the state.</li><li>The state broke up around 1000, but its roads, terraces and cord records foreshadowed the institutions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>When Wari colonists left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerro-baul">Cerro Baúl</a> around 1000, they held a final feast, then burned their brewery and threw their drinking cups into the flames.</p></aside>
    </section>

